---
description: Follow each repo's own rules and hooks
alwaysApply: true
---
Before starting work or asking the user anything, read in order: the repo's agent guide, its binding
rules / decisions file, the project's INDEX.md in the shared working memory, and the newest handoff note.
If a rule or note already answers a question, act on it and cite it; never ask what the rules answer.
Before changing anything in a repo, read and follow its own AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,
decisions log, hooks (.pre-commit-config.yaml, core.hooksPath, .git/hooks) and CI workflows.
Never bypass a hook or gate without the user's explicit yes: no --no-verify, no skipping CI, no
direct pushes of generated or bot-owned files. Branch + PR, never force-push, one repo at a time.

Before driving Autodesk Fusion, hold the per-PC Fusion lock: see section 5 "Fusion lock" in the workstation repo agents/projects-AGENTS.md.
